const faqItems = [
  { question: "How many mg of THC should a beginner take in a Maine edible?", answer: "If you have not used a THC edible before, start at 2.5-5mg of THC total and wait a full two hours before taking more. Maine Revised Statutes Title 28-B §703(1)(F) caps a single serving of a cannabis edible at 10mg of THC, and a single package at 200mg of THC, with a 10% allowable variance. A 10mg gummy can be split in half for a true 5mg starting dose. The most common edible mistake in Maine is taking a second piece at the one-hour mark because the first has not kicked in; two hours is the realistic onset window for most gummies on a full stomach." },
  { question: "Are Maine dispensary edibles lab tested?", answer: "Yes. Every cannabis edible sold at a licensed Maine dispensary is lab tested at an ISO-17025 accredited cannabis lab, and the results are posted to the state's METRC seed-to-sale tracking system. Each batch of edible has a Certificate of Analysis (COA) that lists total THC, total CBD, terpene content, and a contaminant panel (residual solvents, heavy metals, microbials, mycotoxins, pesticides). The COA is available on the dispensary's menu and on the OCP's public-facing product tracker. Maine's testing standards are consistent with mature West Coast markets and stricter than several Northeast peers on the pesticide panel." },
  { question: "How long do Maine cannabis gummies take to kick in?", answer: "Most Maine cannabis gummies take 30-90 minutes to take effect when eaten on a light snack, and 60-120 minutes when eaten on a full meal. The peak effect arrives roughly 2-3 hours after consumption, and the total duration runs 4-8 hours depending on dose, individual metabolism, and tolerance. Sublingual formats (mints, lozenges, oral strips) absorb faster, with onset at 5-15 minutes and duration of 2-4 hours. Beverages typically onset at 15-30 minutes and last 2-4 hours. The single most common edible problem in Maine is impatience; wait the full two hours before redosing." },
  { question: "What is the best edible for sleep in Maine?", answer: "For sleep specifically, a 1:1 or 2:1 THC:CBN edible is the most reliable option. The Maine Lab Snooze Sleep Tablets (100mg THC:200mg CBN, 4-count, ~50mg THC + 100mg CBN per tablet) are the highest-dose sleep edible produced by a Maine operator and are widely stocked across the state. For a milder starting dose, Theory Wellness' Rest line and Sola's RSO Sleep gummies (4:1 CBN:THC) are both effective at 10-20mg THC. CBN is a degraded-THC cannabinoid with sedating properties, and the 1:1 or 2:1 THC:CBN ratio is the most-researched combination for sleep onset and duration. Avoid caffeine and high-sugar edible formats within four hours of bedtime." },
  { question: "Can I have a Maine edible delivered to my home?", answer: "Medical-use delivery is well-established in Maine, but adult-use delivery is limited. Several caregivers and a small number of dispensaries offer delivery to registered MMMP cardholders within a defined service radius (typically 15-30 miles). For adult-use customers, in-store pickup is the default; a small number of operators in the Portland and Bangor metros offer same-day or next-day adult-use delivery through Dutchie, Leafly, or their own e-commerce platform. The OCP has been expanding the adult-use delivery framework in 2025-2026, and statewide adult-use delivery is expected to roll out more broadly through 2026-2027." }
];

